closest-possible: same LRU algorithm as Crystal LRUCache (hit moves to front, miss inserts at front, evicts the tail at capacity, same checksum formula), but the representation is a node array with prev/next indices plus a map index, not heap-allocated nodes with a Hash; keys and values are Ascii max 16/24 instead of String; the LCG is integer last * max_value / IM instead of Crystal float (equal in exact arithmetic, and the run checksum matches); timed rounds use iteration ids offset by warmup, while Crystal numbers run_all ids from 0 (checksum for the timed run still matches). Prep mode runs only the warmup rounds because Crystal has no prepare step.
